# $title

This is your private research book. Agents look for ways to invest in
stocks held $holding. Each idea is written down as a bet before any testing,
with its odds, its size, and the date by which it must prove itself. You
decide, and you place every trade yourself.

## Your daily brief

Each day the agents send you a short brief in chat at $when. Its last line
names the one reply it needs from you, or says that nothing needs deciding.
Nothing is traded and no setting changes until you say so.

## How to reply

Answer in plain words, in chat.

1. Decide on a proposal. Say approve, reject, or override, with your reason
   in your own words.
2. Report what you traded. $sending$account After trading, paste the
   confirmation table from your broker, attach a screenshot, or describe the
   trades in a sentence. The agents show you what they read; say yes if it
   is right.
3. Change a setting. Ask in a sentence, for example a lower risk limit or a
   sector to leave out. The agents show you the change and make it when you
   say yes.
4. Ask anything.

## Where the history is

Everything the agents decided, tested, and traded is kept in the `ledger/`
folder of this book. Lines are only ever added there, never changed.
